import{_ as e,c as o,o as d,a3 as t}from"./chunks/framework.Bsyxd66g.js";const b=JSON.parse('{"title":"Web API server","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"subsystems/web-api-server.md","filePath":"subsystems/web-api-server.md","lastUpdated":1794137243000}'),i={name:"subsystems/web-api-server.md"},c=t('<h1 id="web-api-server" tabindex="-1">Web API server <a class="header-anchor" href="#web-api-server" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Web API server&quot;">​</a></h1><h2 id="responsibility-and-boundaries" tabindex="-1">Responsibility and boundaries <a class="header-anchor" href="#responsibility-and-boundaries" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Responsibility and boundaries&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Owns: the HTTP listener and bind-address fallback, the embedded front-end asset serving, the <code>/api</code> router and its authentication middleware, the response envelope and status-code mapping, request validation, the WebSocket endpoint <code>/api/ws</code> (subscription protocol, log replay, task status, system info polling) and the exact JSON shapes returned to the browser.</li><li>Does not own: the business behavior behind each endpoint (<a href="./sync-pipeline">sync-pipeline.md</a>, <a href="./config-and-persistence">config-and-persistence.md</a>, <a href="./bilibili-client">bilibili-client.md</a>, <a href="./notifications">notifications.md</a>); the SvelteKit app that consumes these endpoints (<a href="./web-ui">web-ui.md</a>).</li><li>Talks to: <code>VersionedConfig</code> (auth token, bind address), <code>DatabaseConnection</code> and <code>Arc&lt;BiliClient&gt;</code> injected as axum <code>Extension</code>s, <code>DownloadTaskManager</code> and <code>LogHelper</code> for the WebSocket, and <code>rust_embed_for_web</code> for the compiled front-end.</li></ul><h2 id="sources-of-truth" tabindex="-1">Sources of truth <a class="header-anchor" href="#sources-of-truth" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Sources of truth&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Authoritative routing: <code>crates/bili_sync/src/api/routes/mod.rs</code> (<code>router</code>, <code>auth</code>). Adding an endpoint means adding a module <code>router()</code> here.</li><li>Authoritative envelope: <code>crates/bili_sync/src/api/wrapper.rs</code> (<code>ApiResponse</code>, <code>ApiError</code>, <code>ValidatedJson</code>) and <code>crates/bili_sync/src/api/error.rs</code> (<code>InnerApiError</code>).</li><li>Authoritative payloads: <code>crates/bili_sync/src/api/request.rs</code> (query/body types) and <code>crates/bili_sync/src/api/response.rs</code> (returned types, plus the <code>serde_*_download_status</code> serializers).</li><li>Authoritative static serving and bind logic: <code>crates/bili_sync/src/task/http_server.rs</code> (<code>http_server</code>, <code>frontend_files</code>, <code>Asset</code>).</li><li>Authoritative WebSocket contract: <code>crates/bili_sync/src/api/routes/ws/mod.rs</code> (<code>EventType</code>, <code>ClientEvent</code>, <code>ServerEvent</code>, <code>WebSocketHandler</code>) and <code>ws/log_helper.rs</code> (<code>LogHelper</code>, <code>MAX_HISTORY_LOGS</code>).</li><li>Forbidden duplicate sources: a second envelope type, error strings duplicated in handlers instead of <code>InnerApiError</code>, or a TypeScript type that contradicts <code>api/response.rs</code>.</li></ul><h2 id="main-paths-change-loci" tabindex="-1">Main paths / change loci <a class="header-anchor" href="#main-paths-change-loci" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Main paths / change loci&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Key entry points: <ul><li><code>crates/bili_sync/src/task/http_server.rs</code> (<code>http_server</code>) — starts axum, embeds <code>web/build</code>.</li><li><code>crates/bili_sync/src/api/routes/mod.rs</code> (<code>router</code>, <code>auth</code>) — path prefix and authentication.</li><li>Route modules: <code>config</code>, <code>me</code>, <code>login</code>, <code>video_sources</code>, <code>videos</code>, <code>dashboard</code>, <code>ws</code>, <code>task</code> under <code>crates/bili_sync/src/api/routes/</code>.</li></ul></li><li>Common edit locations: <ul><li>New endpoint: add a handler + <code>router()</code> in the matching module and merge it in <code>routes/mod.rs</code>.</li><li>New request type: <code>api/request.rs</code>, with <code>#[derive(Validate)]</code> and <code>ValidatedJson</code> in the handler when validation is needed.</li><li>New response shape: <code>api/response.rs</code>; keep the front-end type in <code>web/src/lib/types.ts</code> in sync.</li><li>Event or subscription change: <code>api/routes/ws/mod.rs</code> and <code>web/src/lib/ws.ts</code> together.</li><li>Auth semantics: <code>auth</code> in <code>api/routes/mod.rs</code> only.</li></ul></li><li>Endpoint inventory (all prefixed with <code>/api</code>): <ul><li><code>GET /api/config</code>, <code>PUT /api/config</code>, <code>POST /api/config/notifiers/ping</code>.</li><li><code>GET /api/me/favorites</code>, <code>GET /api/me/collections</code>, <code>GET /api/me/uppers</code>.</li><li><code>POST /api/login/qrcode/generate</code>, <code>GET /api/login/qrcode/poll?qrcode_key=…</code>.</li><li><code>GET /api/video-sources</code>, <code>GET /api/video-sources/details</code>, <code>GET /api/video-sources/{type}/default-path</code>, <code>PUT|DELETE /api/video-sources/{type}/{id}</code>, <code>POST /api/video-sources/{type}/{id}/evaluate</code>, <code>POST /api/video-sources/{type}/{id}/full-sync</code>, <code>POST /api/video-sources/favorites|collections|submissions</code>.</li><li><code>GET /api/videos</code>, <code>GET /api/videos/{id}</code>, <code>POST /api/videos/{id}/redownload</code>, <code>POST /api/videos/{id}/reset-status</code>, <code>POST /api/videos/{id}/update-status</code>, <code>POST /api/videos/reset-status</code>, <code>POST /api/videos/update-status</code>.</li><li><code>POST /api/videos/{id}/redownload</code> rejects an unavailable download lock, invalid video or missing page details; accepted requests return <code>{ started: true }</code> and run asynchronously under the shared download lock. Video deletion, cleanup and clear-and-reset routes are not exposed.</li><li><code>GET /api/videos/{id}/cover</code> serves an authenticated local image or a JSON 404 when unavailable.</li><li><code>GET|POST /api/organization/rules</code>, <code>PUT|DELETE /api/organization/rules/{id}</code>, <code>POST /api/organization/rules/{id}/preview</code>, <code>POST /api/organization/rules/{id}/execute</code>. Movie preview can list candidates without IDs; movie execution requires explicit video IDs.</li><li><code>GET /api/organization/directory?path=…</code> lists subdirectories of an existing absolute server/container path (<code>{ path, parent, entries: [{ path, name }] }</code>, directories only, sorted by name); empty <code>path</code> starts at <code>/</code>. Invalid paths return 400. Behind the same auth middleware; it exposes the server filesystem layout to the logged-in operator, not file contents.</li><li><code>GET /api/dashboard</code> returns <code>DashBoardResponse { recent_videos: [RecentVideoInfo] }</code> — the 5 most-recently-added videos ordered by <code>created_at</code> desc then <code>id</code> desc; each item carries <code>id</code>, <code>name</code>, <code>valid</code>, <code>should_download</code>, the five-slot <code>download_status</code> tuple, and the naive-UTC <code>created_at</code> string (<code>YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS</code>, frontend parses it as UTC). <code>POST /api/task/download</code>, <code>GET /api/ws</code> (WebSocket upgrade).</li></ul></li></ul><h2 id="runtime-paths-and-state-transitions" tabindex="-1">Runtime paths and state transitions <a class="header-anchor" href="#runtime-paths-and-state-transitions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Runtime paths and state transitions&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Trigger / inputs / outputs / interfaces: <ul><li>Inputs: HTTP requests with an <code>Authorization</code> header (or WebSocket subprotocol), JSON bodies, query parameters.</li><li>Outputs: <code>ApiResponse&lt;T&gt;</code> JSON with the HTTP status equal to <code>status_code</code>; embedded static files; WebSocket text frames containing <code>ServerEvent</code>.</li><li>Bind address: <code>VersionedConfig::get().read().bind_address</code>; on bind failure it retries <code>default_bind_address()</code> (<code>0.0.0.0:12345</code>) unless it was already the configured value, logging <code>绑定到地址 {} 失败：{:#}，尝试绑定到默认地址 {}</code>; success logs <code>开始运行管理页：http://{addr}</code>.</li></ul></li><li>Main execution path (source files and named symbols): <ol><li><code>http_server</code> builds <code>router()</code> (the whole <code>/api</code> tree) and adds <code>.fallback_service(get(frontend_files).head(frontend_files))</code>, then <code>Extension(database_connection)</code>, <code>Extension(bili_client)</code>, <code>Extension(log_writer)</code>. Only the <code>/api</code> subtree carries the auth middleware; static assets are served without it.</li><li><code>auth</code> compares the <code>Authorization</code> header to <code>auth_token</code> by exact string equality. If that fails it removes <code>Sec-WebSocket-Protocol</code>, base64-url-safe-no-pad decodes it, and compares the bytes to the token; on success the protocol header is echoed on the response (required by browsers for a WebSocket subprotocol). Otherwise <code>ApiResponse::&lt;()&gt;::unauthorized(&quot;auth token does not match&quot;)</code>.</li><li>Handlers return <code>Result&lt;ApiResponse&lt;T&gt;, ApiError&gt;</code>. <code>ApiError</code> downcasts <code>InnerApiError::NotFound</code> → 404 and <code>BadRequest</code> → 400 (both with the error&#39;s <code>Display</code> text as <code>message</code>); every other error becomes 500 with <code>{:#}</code> formatting. <code>ApiResponse::ok</code> sets <code>status_code = 200</code>, <code>data</code> present, no <code>message</code>; error constructors leave <code>data</code> absent and set <code>message</code>. Both optional fields are skipped when <code>None</code>.</li><li><code>ValidatedJson&lt;T&gt;</code> extracts JSON and then runs <code>validator::Validate</code>, mapping failures to <code>InnerApiError::BadRequest(e.to_string())</code>. <code>StatusUpdate</code> restricts <code>status_index</code> to <code>0..=4</code> and <code>status_value</code> to <code>STATUS_OK</code> or <code>STATUS_NOT_STARTED</code> (<code>utils::validation::validate_status_value</code>); path fields use <code>validate_path</code> (non-empty absolute).</li><li><code>frontend_files</code> resolves the request path; empty or unknown paths fall back to <code>index.html</code> (SPA routing). Responses carry <code>Content-Type</code> from the embedded file, <code>Cache-Control: no-cache</code>, and <code>ETag</code> = <code>content.hash()</code>. A matching <code>If-None-Match</code> returns 304; <code>HEAD</code> returns headers only. Debug builds return the raw file; release builds pick <code>br</code> then <code>gzip</code> from <code>Accept-Encoding</code> and return 406 <code>Client must support gzip or brotli compression</code> when neither is acceptable.</li><li>WebSocket <code>websocket_handler</code> upgrades and splits the socket: a sender task forwards <code>mpsc</code> events, a receiver task parses <code>ClientEvent</code>. <code>EventType</code> is <code>camelCase</code>: <code>logs</code>, <code>tasks</code>, <code>sysInfo</code>; <code>ServerEvent</code> is a <code>camelCase</code> enum with the same names (<code>{&quot;logs&quot;: &quot;...&quot;}</code>, <code>{&quot;tasks&quot;: {...}}</code>, <code>{&quot;sysInfo&quot;: {...}}</code>).</li><li>On <code>subscribe logs</code>, the handler first replays <code>LogHelper</code> history (up to <code>MAX_HISTORY_LOGS = 200</code> entries) and then chains the broadcast stream (channel capacity 30, created in <code>main::init</code>); the replay and live stream are one <code>ServerEvent::Logs</code> sequence.</li><li>On <code>subscribe tasks</code>, it streams <code>DownloadTaskManager::get().subscribe()</code> (a <code>watch</code> channel) as <code>TaskStatus { is_running, last_run, last_finish, next_run }</code>.</li><li>On <code>subscribe sysInfo</code>, the connection registers in a global <code>DashMap</code>. A single process-wide poller is started when the first subscriber arrives and cancelled when the last leaves; it ticks every 2 seconds and does the <code>sysinfo</code> refresh on a blocking thread, then fans out to every subscriber. <code>used_cpu</code> is the global CPU usage, <code>process_cpu</code> is the process usage divided by CPU count, and disk totals sum physical disks excluding <code>overlay</code>, <code>tmpfs</code>, <code>sysfs</code>, <code>proc</code>.</li></ol></li><li>State ownership, transitions and persistence: <ul><li>Nothing in this layer is persisted; it reads the config and database and mutates them only through the owning modules.</li><li><code>SysInfo</code> timestamps are <code>Utc::now().timestamp_millis()</code>.</li><li>Per-connection state is the registration UUID plus per-subscription <code>CancellationToken</code>s, all dropped on disconnect.</li></ul></li></ul><h2 id="constraints-and-failures" tabindex="-1">Constraints and failures <a class="header-anchor" href="#constraints-and-failures" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Constraints and failures&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Invariants: <ul><li>Every <code>/api</code> handler must be behind <code>auth</code>; adding a route outside <code>router()</code> bypasses authentication.</li><li>For JSON envelopes, HTTP status must equal <code>status_code</code> in the body; clients rely on both.</li><li>JSON endpoints under <code>/api</code> return <code>ApiResponse</code> for front-end error mapping. The authenticated cover endpoint returns image bytes on success and JSON on errors.</li><li><code>download_status</code> is serialized as a five-element <code>[u32; 5]</code> array by <code>serde_video_download_status</code>/<code>serde_page_download_status</code>; never expose the packed <code>u32</code>.</li></ul></li><li>Failure modes and recovery: <ul><li>Missing/incorrect token → 401 <code>auth token does not match</code>. There is no automatic redirect or token prompt on that response; the UI surfaces it as a toast and the user re-enters the token in <code>/settings</code>.</li><li>Bind failure → automatic fallback to <code>0.0.0.0:12345</code>; if that also fails the task ends, which cancels the whole program (<code>main::spawn_task</code> logs <code>「HTTP 服务」异常结束…</code>).</li><li>Handler errors are logged by the caller chain and returned as 500 with the error display; there is no retry at the HTTP layer.</li><li>WebSocket drops are handled by the client (<code>web/src/lib/ws.ts</code> reconnects up to 5 times); the server simply cancels that connection&#39;s tasks.</li><li>Release builds without <code>Accept-Encoding</code> support get 406 instead of uncompressed assets — a reverse proxy must not strip the header.</li><li><code>reset-status</code> with <code>force: true</code> clears stale completed bits; without it, <code>reset_failed</code> only resets non-zero, non-OK subtasks.</li></ul></li><li>Compatibility / migration behavior: <ul><li>Route paths and JSON field names are consumed by the bundled front-end; renaming requires matching <code>web/src/lib/api.ts</code>/<code>types.ts</code> changes in the same commit.</li><li><code>VideoSourceDetail</code> and <code>UpdateVideoSourceRequest</code> are <code>camelCase</code>; most other payloads are snake_case. Keep that split when adding fields.</li><li><code>GET /api/videos</code> pairs <code>page</code>/<code>page_size</code>: if either is missing, both defaults are used (<code>0</code> and <code>10</code>).</li></ul></li></ul><h2 id="forbidden-patterns-and-common-mistakes" tabindex="-1">Forbidden patterns and common mistakes <a class="header-anchor" href="#forbidden-patterns-and-common-mistakes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Forbidden patterns and common mistakes&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Forbidden: adding business logic to handlers; handlers should translate the request and delegate to the owning module.</li><li>Forbidden: returning a raw <code>(StatusCode, Json&lt;…&gt;)</code> tuple; it breaks the envelope.</li><li>Forbidden: logging or echoing the <code>auth_token</code>.</li><li>Common mistake: assuming static assets require the token. Only <code>/api</code> is authenticated; the SPA is public and asks for the token itself.</li><li>Common mistake: assuming the token is sent as a Bearer token. It is compared verbatim, so the header must be exactly the token value.</li><li>Common mistake: assuming any <code>Sec-WebSocket-Protocol</code> value works; it must be the token encoded with <code>BASE64_URL_SAFE_NO_PAD</code>, and the server echoes the header back.</li><li>Common mistake: assuming <code>/api/videos</code> filters by local date. <code>created_from</code>/<code>created_to</code> are compared against <code>datetime(created_at, &#39;localtime&#39;)</code>, so the caller supplies local wall-clock strings.</li><li>Common mistake: assuming <code>GET /api/video-sources</code> returns persisted watch-later rows. When the table is empty it synthesizes <code>{ id: 1, name: &quot;稍后再看&quot; }</code>; deleting <code>watch_later</code> is rejected as a bad request.</li><li>Common mistake: assuming <code>POST /api/video-sources/{type}/{id}/full-sync</code> only touches the database. With <code>delete_local: true</code> it also removes local directories and reports failures in <code>warnings</code> instead of failing.</li><li>Common mistake: expecting <code>SysInfo</code> to include <code>used_disk</code>. The Rust struct has <code>total_disk</code>/<code>available_disk</code> only (see the front-end page for the consequence).</li><li>Common mistake: expecting the socket to push immediately without a <code>subscribe</code> message. Each event type must be subscribed explicitly, and history is replayed only once per subscription.</li></ul><h2 id="how-to-verify" tabindex="-1">How to verify <a class="header-anchor" href="#how-to-verify" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;How to verify&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Start the binary and check the startup log: <code>开始运行管理页：http://&lt;addr&gt;</code>; with a deliberately occupied port, confirm the fallback warning and that the UI still answers on <code>12345</code>.</li><li>Auth: <code>curl -i http://127.0.0.1:12345/api/config</code> → 401 envelope; repeat with <code>-H &quot;Authorization: &lt;token&gt;&quot;</code> → 200 with the config.</li><li>Envelope: request a missing video id and confirm HTTP 404 with <code>{&quot;status_code&quot;:404,&quot;message&quot;:&quot;Primary key not found: &lt;id&gt;&quot;}</code>.</li><li>Validation: <code>POST /api/videos/1/update-status</code> with <code>status_index: 9</code> or <code>status_value: 3</code> → 400 from <code>ValidatedJson</code>.</li><li>Static serving: <code>curl -I</code> on <code>/</code> and on an unknown SPA path (both 200 with an <code>ETag</code>), then repeat with <code>If-None-Match</code> → 304.</li><li>WebSocket: connect to <code>ws://127.0.0.1:12345/api/ws?</code> with <code>Sec-WebSocket-Protocol: &lt;base64url token&gt;</code>, send <code>{&quot;subscribe&quot;:&quot;logs&quot;}</code>, confirm the 200-entry history replay followed by live logs; subscribe <code>sysInfo</code> and confirm ~2-second cadence; close the last sysInfo subscriber and confirm polling stops (CPU usage drops).</li><li>Existing automated checks: <code>cargo test -p bili_sync</code>, <code>cargo clippy -- -D warnings</code>, <code>cargo +nightly fmt --check</code>.</li></ul>',15),s=[c];function a(n,r,l,u,h,p){return d(),o("div",null,s)}const g=e(i,[["render",a]]);export{b as __pageData,g as default};
